items: policy-selftest-stages-into-the-shared-index
paths: file:tests/e2e/policy-single-source.sh file:tests/e2e/policy-selftest-residue-gate.sh file:scripts/smoke-ci.ssc file:.gitignore file:tests/BUGS.md
scope: |
  `policy-single-source.sh --self-test` stages its fixture into the SHARED index; a killed run
  leaves an intent-to-add entry for a deleted file and `git rebase` then refuses to start for
  whoever owns that checkout (reported in the room 2026-08-14). Fix: the self-test drives a COPY
  of the index through GIT_INDEX_FILE, so no signal can leave anything there; trap for the file
  on disk; .gitignore so a SIGKILL leftover is inert. New gate interrupts a real run at a known
  point with SIGTERM and SIGKILL and asserts `git rebase` still starts, with its own control on
  the unfixed script.
next: smoke-ci in the worktree, then rebase, repoint fixed-in, push
